3168       
3169       *----------------- Data on Physical Fitness -----------------*
3170       | These measurements were made on men involved in a physical |
3171       | fitness course at N.C. State University. |
3172       | Only selected variables of |
3173       | Oxygen (oxygen intake, ml per kg body weight per minute), |
3174       | Runtime (time to run 1.5 miles in minutes), and |
3175       | RunPulse (heart rate while running) are used. |
3176       | Certain values were changed to missing for the analysis. |
3177       *------------------------------------------------------------*;
3178       data Fitness1;
3179       input Oxygen RunTime RunPulse @@;
3180       datalines;

NOTE: SAS went to a new line when INPUT statement reached past the end of a line.
NOTE: The data set WORK.FITNESS1 has 31 observations and 3 variables.

3197       ;
3198       proc mi data=Fitness1 seed=3237851 noprint out=outmi;
3199       var Oxygen RunTime RunPulse;
3200       run;

WARNING: The default number of imputations has been changed from 5 to 25.
NOTE: The EM algorithm (MLE) converges in 12 iterations.
NOTE: The EM algorithm (posterior mode) converges in 7 iterations.
NOTE: The data set WORK.OUTMI has 775 observations and 4 variables.

3201       proc reg data=outmi outest=outreg covout noprint;
3202       model Oxygen= RunTime RunPulse;
3203       by _Imputation_;
3204       run;

NOTE: Interactivity disabled with BY processing.
NOTE: The data set WORK.OUTREG has 100 observations and 10 variables.

3205       proc print data=outreg(obs=8);
3206       var _Imputation_ _Type_ _Name_
3207       Intercept RunTime RunPulse;
3208       title 'Parameter Estimates from Imputed Data Sets';
3209       run;

NOTE: There were 8 observations read from the data set WORK.OUTREG.
NOTE: The PROCEDURE PRINT printed page 272.

3210       proc mianalyze data=outreg;
3211       modeleffects Intercept RunTime RunPulse;
3212       run;

NOTE: The PROCEDURE MIANALYZE printed page 273.

